{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "01422",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 0.52,
      "end_seconds": 7.35,
      "duration_seconds": 6.83,
      "text": "Doctor, I've checked them in and done the preliminary measurements, I'll hand them over when you ask."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 9.18,
      "end_seconds": 13.2,
      "duration_seconds": 4.02,
      "text": "Okay, thanks. Hi, how can I help today?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 14.85,
      "end_seconds": 21.0,
      "duration_seconds": 6.15,
      "text": "Good afternoon, doctor. I look after them so I thought I'd come."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 22.53,
      "end_seconds": 25.91,
      "duration_seconds": 3.38,
      "text": "I'm here because of yellow eyes."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 26.65,
      "end_seconds": 28.04,
      "duration_seconds": 1.39,
      "text": "Since when exactly?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 32.1,
      "end_seconds": 37.84,
      "duration_seconds": 5.74,
      "text": "Ever since... since this morning, really. I've also had no appetite."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 50.76,
      "end_seconds": 55.49,
      "duration_seconds": 4.73,
      "text": "So, are you taking anything regularly, including from the pharmacy?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 56.8,
      "end_seconds": 61.28,
      "duration_seconds": 4.48,
      "text": "I take omeprazole, 20 milligrams, once a day."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_3",
      "role": "CAREGIVER",
      "start_seconds": 65.78,
      "end_seconds": 73.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.88,
      "text": "It's meant to be once a day, though I don't see she take it every time."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 74.36,
      "end_seconds": 78.41,
      "duration_seconds": 4.05,
      "text": "I take paracetamol, 650 milligrams, when needed."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 79.22,
      "end_seconds": 80.47,
      "duration_seconds": 1.25,
      "text": "Is that long-standing?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 82.2,
      "end_seconds": 89.58,
      "duration_seconds": 7.38,
      "text": "About about three months. I'd been on diclofenac, not any more though, I stopped."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 90.39,
      "end_seconds": 91.62,
      "duration_seconds": 1.23,
      "text": "Are you active?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 93.49,
      "end_seconds": 96.5,
      "duration_seconds": 3.01,
      "text": "I walk the dog every morning."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 108.86,
      "end_seconds": 113.15,
      "duration_seconds": 4.29,
      "text": "Are you allergic to anything? Any allergies to medicines or foods?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 114.05,
      "end_seconds": 125.7,
      "duration_seconds": 11.65,
      "text": "Hmm, there was some antibiotic, I was told I was allergic. But I couldn't tell you what it was called or what it did."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 126.6,
      "end_seconds": 129.8,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "Has anyone in your family had anything serious?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 133.51,
      "end_seconds": 138.85,
      "duration_seconds": 5.34,
      "text": "Ah, my uncle has high cholesterol. My father had bowel cancer."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 139.94,
      "end_seconds": 143.74,
      "duration_seconds": 3.8,
      "text": "Tell me about any past illnesses or ongoing conditions."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 147.91,
      "end_seconds": 158.27,
      "duration_seconds": 10.36,
      "text": "I have acid reflux, for five years. I've got arthritis in my knees. I told my wife I'd come today."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 160.2,
      "end_seconds": 172.53,
      "duration_seconds": 12.33,
      "text": "Mm, okay. Alright, arthritis in your knees, that matches what I have here. Okay, have you had any bleeding, itching or severe abdominal pain?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 174.29,
      "end_seconds": 188.1,
      "duration_seconds": 13.81,
      "text": "No, um, no bleeding, no itching, no severe abdominal pain. I did have tiredness at one point, but that went away on its own."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 189.27,
      "end_seconds": 192.9,
      "duration_seconds": 3.63,
      "text": "Have you had any vomiting blood or fever?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 194.55,
      "end_seconds": 200.5,
      "duration_seconds": 5.95,
      "text": "Let me think, no vomiting blood or fever, none of it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 201.68,
      "end_seconds": 205.28,
      "duration_seconds": 3.6,
      "text": "Anything with your nerves, like weakness or numbness?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 207.09,
      "end_seconds": 210.49,
      "duration_seconds": 3.4,
      "text": "No, uh, that's all normal."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 212.55,
      "end_seconds": 215.84,
      "duration_seconds": 3.29,
      "text": "Anything on the skin I should know about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 216.51,
      "end_seconds": 218.57,
      "duration_seconds": 2.06,
      "text": "No, skin's been fine."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "NURSE",
      "start_seconds": 220.08,
      "end_seconds": 228.29,
      "duration_seconds": 8.21,
      "text": "Doctor, I've got the readings for you. Temperature is 36.7 degrees, pulse 72, blood pressure 117 over 70."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 229.53,
      "end_seconds": 230.96,
      "duration_seconds": 1.43,
      "text": "Good, thank you."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 232.17,
      "end_seconds": 235.81,
      "duration_seconds": 3.64,
      "text": "I'll examine you in a second, make yourself comfortable."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 237.01,
      "end_seconds": 239.92,
      "duration_seconds": 2.91,
      "text": "Stay as you are for a moment."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 247.18,
      "end_seconds": 254.89,
      "duration_seconds": 7.71,
      "text": "The whites of your eyes are yellow and the liver edge is tender under the right ribs."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 260.06,
      "end_seconds": 273.8,
      "duration_seconds": 13.74,
      "text": "Okay, that's enough for me. Right, here's what I'm thinking. It points towards an acute viral hepatitis. It could also be a drug-related liver problem, so we'll keep that open."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0035",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 274.92,
      "end_seconds": 278.12,
      "duration_seconds": 3.2,
      "text": "I'm scared it's something bad. Is it?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0036",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 279.56,
      "end_seconds": 297.37,
      "duration_seconds": 17.81,
      "text": "Nothing I've seen today points to an emergency. It looks like an acute viral hepatitis, but I'd like to confirm. Let me just check I've got this right. You've had yellow eyes, since this morning, and no fever or severe abdominal pain."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0037",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 298.65,
      "end_seconds": 300.17,
      "duration_seconds": 1.52,
      "text": "Yes, that's right."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0038",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 302.01,
      "end_seconds": 333.46,
      "duration_seconds": 31.45,
      "text": "I'd like to arrange an ultrasound of the liver for jaundice. I'm going to order liver blood tests, for jaundice. No alcohol at all and avoid paracetamol and other painkillers unless we say. Don't skip meals, and try to eat smaller portions more often through the day. Let's get you seen by the liver clinic, I'll arrange the letter. Please come and see me after the results. That's everything on my side. Anything you're unsure about?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0039",
      "speaker_id": "person_4",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 335.05,
      "end_seconds": 337.3,
      "duration_seconds": 2.25,
      "text": "Alright, thanks, take care."
    }
  ]
}